<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Richard Squires</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1940</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Richard Squires was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> from 1919 to 1923 and from 1928 to 1932. His governments were dogged by allegations of corruption, and in April 1932, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, a crowd protesting against him stormed the Colonial Building in St John's. He lost the election that year, and in 1934 the dominion gave up self-government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-squires.jpg" alt="Richard Squires" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Photo Company Collection · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Richard_Squires_LOC_npcc.05059_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
